Bolivia,BOL,2.  Does sovereignty confer on states authority over cyber infrastructure located in their respective territories and over the actions they take with respect to that infrastructure?,Yes,"¶ 2. A state’s sovereignty can therefore be violated well via attacks from cyberspace, by non-state organizations, and by insufficient international regulation that is hard to enforce. As a result, states must monitor and control cyber infrastructures in their territory or those operating under their flag without necessarily being inside their geographical boundaries.","OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Bolivia, pg. 7, Question 10, ¶ 2 (2019).",/static/documents/24_bolivia-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,This answer can be reasonably inferred from the statement,
