Finland,FIN,10. Can state cyber operations that deny access to or degrade data in the control of another State constitute a violation of sovereignty as a rule?,Yes,"Similarly, a non-consensual intrusion in the computer networks and systems that rely on the cyber infrastructure in another State’s territory may amount to a violation of that State’s sovereignty.  ...other relevant considerations include whether an intrusion in the cyber infrastructure triggers a loss of functionality of the equipment relying on it, or modifies or deletes information belonging to the target State, or to private actors in its territory.",International Law and Cyberspace: Finland’s National Positions,https://perma.cc/M5DA-YSE6,,
Finland,FIN,10(a) Do state sponsored ransomware operations violate the sovereignty of another State?,Silent,,,,,
