Guatemala,GTM,2(b) Is the exercise of such sovereign authority subject to international human rights law and other fundamental freedoms?,Yes.,"Yes: the current fields of international law apply to the existing proposals and draft legislation, together with the strategies and policies related to national cybersecurity, including the prohibition of the use of force, the right of legitimate defense, international humanitarian law, and human rights.","OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guatemala,",/static/documents/25_guatemala-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
Guatemala,GTM,"3. Is sovereignty a stand-alone, primary rule of international law, the breach of which can incur international responsibility?",Ambiguous,"Consequently, a State participating in a specific cyber operations violates a country’s sovereignty if, in the course of a cyber attack, it takes certain information from another State’s cyber realm, even when no harm that could affect equipment or the human rights of a person or persons is caused.","OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guatemala,",/static/documents/25_guatemala-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
