Guyana,GUY,1. Is sovereignty a foundational principle of the international legal order?,Silent,,,,,
Guyana,GUY,2. Does sovereignty confer on states authority over cyber infrastructure located in their respective territories and over the actions they take with respect to that infrastructure?,Yes,Q9. States have a right to exercise their territorial jurisdiction over cyber activities within their territories. Q8. Cyber infrastructure located in areas covered by the territorial sovereignty is protected against interference by other States.,OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guyana,/static/documents/29_guyana-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
Guyana,GUY,"2(a) Does sovereignty encompass the right of a state to protect cyber infrastructure and safeguard cyber activity that is located in, or takes place on, its territory?",Ambiguous,Q9. States have a right to exercise their territorial jurisdiction over cyber activities within their territories. Q8. Cyber infrastructure located in areas covered by the territorial sovereignty is protected against interference by other States.,OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guyana,/static/documents/29_guyana-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
Guyana,GUY,2(b) Is the exercise of such sovereign authority subject to international human rights law and other fundamental freedoms?,Silent,,,,,
Guyana,GUY,"3. Is sovereignty a stand-alone, primary rule of international law, the breach of which can incur international responsibility?",Yes,"Q8. If a State’s sovereignty is violated, it amounts to a breach of international law.”",OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guyana,/static/documents/29_guyana-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
Guyana,GUY,3(a) Can violations of sovereignty not amounting to prohibited interventions constitute internationally wrongful acts?,Yes,"Q8. This protection is not limited to activities amounting to an unjustified use of force, to an armed attack, or to a prohibited intervention.",OAS Inter-American Juridical Committee Questionnaire - Response by Guyana,/static/documents/29_guyana-oas-inter-american-juridical-committee-questionnaire.pdf,,
