Ireland,IRL,7. Can state cyber operations that cause a loss to computer functionality in another State’s territory constitute a violation of sovereignty as a rule?,Yes.,"¶6. A violation of a state’s sovereignty may arise where a cyber-operation attributable to another state causes physical damage to ICT or other infrastructure (whether or not in state ownership or control), functional impairment to such infrastructure, interference with data, and/or secondary effects.",Ireland Position Paper on the Application of International Law in Cyberspace,https://perma.cc/K2UL-4HYB,,
