Kenya,KEN,1.  Is sovereignty a foundational principle of the international legal order?,Yes,"The UN Charter forms a strong foundation for the interpretation of existing international laws underlined by inter alia the principles of State sovereignty, sovereign equality, and settlement of international disputes by peaceful means. It is the Charter’s emphasis on these principles that is fully aligned with Kenya’s peaceful stance in international affairs.",UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,,
