United Kingdom,GBR,10(b) Can state cyber operations against data residing in cloud servers outside of a State’s territorial jurisdiction constitute a violation of sovereignty as a rule?,No,¶19. The United Kingdom does not consider that the general concept of sovereignty by itself provides a sufficient or clear basis for extrapolating a specific rule or additional prohibition for cyber conduct going beyond that of non-intervention referred to above.,UNGA Official Compendium of Voluntary National Contributions,https://perma.cc/UD7M-5NA7,,
